{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-FAC-factory-pipeline.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-FAC (campaign c2-resume, x86-main; owner Claude Opus; worker Codex) — the MoE inference-engine factory pipeline (glue over existing CCs)\nUser goal: \"a software factory that takes an MoE model, inspects the stats, inspects the system, and builds an inference engine that runs the model in much less memory; accuracy roughly the same; load time/TTFT/tok-s may change; KV-cache techniques allowed.\"\nExisting components (READ their READMEs; reuse, do not reimplement): cc/model_inspect (model-stats/0), cc/resource_observe (resource-sample/0) + cc/engine_handoff/hosts/*.json (host profiles), cc/moe_planner (plans + emitted lab tests; PLANNER.md rules), cc/build_engine (Build CC v2: --patch, --cmake-define, --extra-target, --linkage), component patches cc/q8_reuse (accepted D029), cc/kv_quant_fix (T-KVB2, pending GPU verification), cc/pap (placement-aware precision recipe; pending), bin/lab (submit/run with input identity + embedded test defs), cc/engine_handoff/envelopes.py (proposal/admit/result), cc/nsys_decode (profile breakdown).\nDeliver cc/factory/factory.py with stages, each writing a JSON artifact into a run directory (artifacts/factory/<run-id>/): `inspect` (model_inspect) -> `system` (resource_observe once + host profile) -> `plan` (moe_planner with budget args) -> `recipe` (for each selected plan: model transform steps (e.g. llama-quantize --tensor-type recipe from cc/pap, with input/output hashes to be filled), engine build args (base commit + ordered patch list from a components registry file cc/factory/components.json with status per component: accepted/pending/rejected and evidence decision IDs; only accepted components by default, `--include-pending` opt-in), runtime argv) -> `build` (calls build_engine.py; supports --dry-run) -> `measure` (submits lab job from the plan's emitted