uild_record.claims.image_config_id` [declared]: \"sha256:cf383f82e33130ce1be424b4c88a78ed12d8a693406b0c3b7ddb61afed0612d1\"\nexperiments/handoff-real/facts.md:31:- `build_record.claims.archive_sha256` [declared]: \"e910feaea3d12c511ce1caddcf5d2a1b072e2a37dfadb143ede7d709f9598aa1\"\nexperiments/handoff-real/facts.md:32:- `build_record.claims.archive_bytes` [declared]: 2210015232\nexperiments/handoff-real/facts.md:33:- `build_record.claims.executable_sha256` [declared]: {\"/app/llama-bench\": \"5e0ab8edefe81093fc8df5d489d629b8a02a755c5dbdae4db18cbe9035be04d6\", \"/app/llama-cli\": \"64b0d6833da5b7d3b3604067bef2fc01f9c42e50ed3e6e24aaf918ec20c9ac04\", \"/app/llama-completion\": \"e019cf44193545e8316015b4bae16dc19c709c460a0bfd5a4a386e56391400c3\", \"/app/llama-eval-callback\": \"bb3f8b38288100ee248cfa2a4b5a9e5e86cf85b8e12a101ac96a536202cb5471\", \"/app/llama-perplexity\": \"aa7ec61d95fb674005cca2f65b74a82d4588bb5b1bbdedf61f9a294da01d99dc\", \"/app/llama-server\": \"3a385482c21a40febee7ef9be8727d3724a594e6c51b3afa127711a259ac257a\", \"/app/llama-tokenize\": \"684063b67410fb7fd87b777f9b86b355daef251f71269d5fb49d57cef1b45486\"}\nexperiments/handoff-real/facts.md:34:- `build_record.claims.source_commit` [declared]: \"31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37\"\nexperiments/handoff-real/facts.md:35:- `build_record.claims.base_image_digests` [declared]: {\"devel\": \"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04@sha256:520292dbb4f755fd360766059e62956e9379485d9e073bbd2f6e3c20c270ed66\", \"runtime\": \"nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime-ubuntu24.04@sha256:ebef3c171eeef0298e4eb2e4be843105edf3b8b0ac45e0b43acee358e8046867\"}\ndecisions/D010-kl-quality-check.md:5:Interpretation: Q8_0 is a small but statistically detectable quality loss (paired PPL ratio is >4 sigma above 1); it is NOT bit-equal. It passes the provisional 1% PPL tripwire but must be reported as \"representation change with measured paired drift\", never as computation-preserving. Q4_K_M fails the 1% tripwire.\ndecisions/D032-pap-and-planner-validation-protocol.md:3:Accept PAP{K}_{q} as a \"better memory/speed point\" if decode median >= +5% vs mixE4K at the same K AND KLD <= 0.08 (2x mixE4K's 0.040; D013 Q4_K_M uniform is 0.078 at higher memory). imatrix effect = KLD(pap24_q3) vs KLD(pap24_q3_noimat). Classification: representation trade-off (NOT computation-preserving).\ndecisions/D024-static-hot-rejected.md:2:Claim category: failed candidate (engine code) + methodology. Evidence: evidence/claude-code.jsonl task X4; artifacts/x4-shot/correct/{off,lru384,hot325,hot487}.{out,err}; image llamacpp-shot2 (run_ref sha256:7040afcd..., config sha256:8edec18d..., patch cc/moe_static_hot/static-hot.patch sha256 0d91a155...). Build record shot-2 status=failed at stage linkage (symbol tools unavailable in runtime image; ldd OK) — binaries otherwise identified (tools hashed, archive saved).\ndecisions/D016-image-identity-confusion.md:6:Lesson (methodology + Manager): identity checks must be performed by an independent observer on the delivered bytes; a record written by the producer is a claim. Two CCs written independently agreed on field names but not on meaning.\nCHECKPOINT-1.md:3:Active: codex-A (Strata map), codex-B (claims+tests) running; downloads: llama.cpp source clone, nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel pull.\ncc/pap/README.md:43:The imatrix uses only the first 100 processed TRAIN chunks; TEST is not used for calibration. It is GGUF format despite the requested `.imatrix` suffix. `MANIFEST.json` records the imatrix metadata, completed chunks, TRAIN and TEST SHA256 hashes, source and output hashes, sizes, and each tensor's actual type and dimensions. `logs/imatrix.log` records the run; calibration start/end files record UTC timestamps. The train/test distinction is dataset provenance, not a claim of zero overlapping natural-language strings.\ncc/pap/README.md:58:Verified type placement, byte reductions, calibration provenance, and content hashes are factory properties. The hypothesis is that smaller CPU expert weights reduce DRAM traffic during decode; speedup need not scale with file size because kernels, routing, caching, and GPU work also contribute. File size does not establish resident host RAM or VRAM. Calibration is intended to reduce low-bit quality loss; that benefit must be measured against the controls. Do not claim throughput improvement, memory residency savings, acceptable quality for all variants, or an imatrix quality improvement without completed corresponding lab results. A WikiText CPU sanity KLD, if present, supports only that model and dataset, not task-level quality.\ncc/pap/README.md:80:Remaining work for the orchestrator: register and execute the 22 GPU lab tests, provide the existing mixE4K baseline beside the outputs, and compare runtime throughput, memory, and quality before making performance or quality claims. No GPU decode or other model KLD result is claimed. Production and verification finished before the 50-minute checkpoint.\ndecisions/D026-c1-q8reuse-protocol.md:1:# D026 — C1 q8_reuse (computation-preserving engine change) — protocol frozen BEFORE results\ndecisions/D026-c1-q8reuse-protocol.md:7:Classification if accepted: full-engine code gain (computation-preserving), discrete RTX 5070 Ti only, this model/workload.\nSTART-HERE.md:9:- `evidence/*.jsonl` — raw per-agent streams (intent/started/outcome); `index/ops.jsonl` merged; `lab/jobs/*` job/attempt state + results; `experiments/` summaries; `claims/paper-claims.md` (15 source-supported claims, none tested yet).\ncc/hybrid_split/README.md:95:latency is not claimed to be strictly proportional to the number of cold IDs.\ncc/hybrid_split/README.md:136:  source/scheduler design claim, not a measured transfer trace.\ncc/hybrid_split/README.md:165:`-c 4096`, and trim hot experts if necessary before making an equal-MiB claim.\ncc/moe_planner/PLANNER.md:84:  computation-preserving improvements. [D009](../../decisions/D009-representation-screen.md),\ncc/moe_planner/PLANNER.md:215:footprint