itting rows, and the frontier within each labelled class. The global comparison is a descriptive pooled view; it does not combine discrete-only measurements into transferable claims. Always consult the class column and class frontier. Comparing workloads or quality references that differ may be meaningless even within one class.\ncc/memory_pareto/README.md:38:This tool establishes **no statistical significance**, uncertainty bounds, speed stability, quality equivalence, or causal improvement. It uses exact input values without tolerance, confidence intervals or significance tests. A frontier is relative only to supplied observations and these objectives, not proof of general optimality. Host memory, PP, Top1 and PPL ratio are contextual columns, not optimization axes. Discrete-only rows remain labelled; neither they nor mixed/unclassified rows establish transferable savings. Fair claims require matched workloads, hardware, model/quality references and memory accounting, reviewed outside this script.\ndecisions/D021-gpu-budget-shim-qualified.md:2:Claim category: infrastructure/fixture validation. NOT a hard device-memory boundary.\ndecisions/D022-static-vs-moecache-matched.md:2:Claim category: runtime-placement/offload trade-off between two EXISTING llama.cpp 31288c9c6 features. Not an engine-code gain.\nassignments/T-E-handoff-tool.md:7:   - `facts --build-record R --archive A --model-config C [--gguf G]` -> facts.json + facts.md: only OBSERVED facts (archive sha256/bytes recomputed, build-record claims, GGUF arch/expert_count/expert_used_count/block_count/file_type/context_length read from header, HF config values), each fact tagged observed|declared|missing; unresolved list.\ndecisions/D023-novmm-engine-under-budget.md:2:Claim category: infrastructure/methodology validation. Evidence: evidence/claude-code.jsonl task X3; artifacts/x3-shim/probe/{c4096-b0,c4096-novmm1,cap900-ngl99,cap900-auto}.{jsonl,out}.\nCHECKPOINT-2.md:4:Pending: read Codex outputs (T-C instrume