s a Markdown table sorted by ascending GPU MiB (unknown memory last), followed by a terminal ASCII scatter of GPU MiB versus KLD. It writes `pareto.md` and `pareto.json` beside the script by default. `--output-dir artifacts/codexI` selects another assignment-permitted destination. Reports are overwritten on reruns. Nothing is written to the input paths. No network, Docker, or third-party runtime packages are used.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe primary input is `experiments/memory/configs.csv`, resolved relative to the campaign root, with these required headers:\n\n```csv\nconfig,desc,class,gpu_mib,host_mib,tg_ts,pp_ts,kld,top1_pct,ppl_ratio,notes\n```\n\n`class` must be `transferable`, `discrete-only`, or `mixed`. Supply the orchestrator's classifications; the script does not validate scientific transferability. Memory is MiB; TG and PP are tokens per second. KLD is smaller-is-better. Top1 is a percentage; PPL ratio is supplied relative to the experiment's stated reference. Neither is converted into KLD. Empty cells, NA, N/A, null, none, NaN and nonfinite numbers become unavailable, never zero. Invalid numbers, negative values, invalid classes, and percentages above 100 are errors. Zero is valid. Notes should identify workloads, hardware, model, measurement method and quality reference. Rows are individual observations; repeated names or exact metric ties are preserved.\n\nIf the default CSV is absent, the script reads `lab/jobs/*/att-*/result.json`, the corresponding `job.json` (`spec.model`), and `lab/tests/*.json` (test-specific `model_file`, args and env). `--lab-root` overrides this fallback root. An explicitly supplied CSV path that is absent is an error; an invalid or empty existing CSV never triggers fallback.\n\nFallback accepts completed attempts and successful, nonpartial tests only. It emits a separate row per benchmark sample record or quality test; it never joins observations across tests, attempts, models or workloads. GPU MiB means `mem.gpu_peak_mib`, **not** baseline-subtracted delta; host MiB means `host_cgroup_peak_mib`. TG requires zero prompt tokens and positive generated tokens; PP requires zero generated tokens and positive prompt tokens. Combined PP+TG samples supply neither speed objective. `avg_ts` supplies speed; repeated `samples_ts` are not independently analyzed. Raw PPL and its stderr are recorded in notes, but no PPL ratio or KLD is invented. Fallback classification is explicitly `unclassified`, so these rows cannot support transferable claims. Job/test/sample identifiers and source result paths are retained. Attempts are not averaged or deduplicated.\n\n## Frontier and budget\n# Campaign c1 — start here (wrap-up snapshot, 2026-11-09)\nGoal (user, latest): methodology + tools for fitting a very large MoE (~500 GB weights -> 128 GB unified memory + 4 TB SSD) at similar accuracy and acceptable tokens/s. Proxy: ibm-granite/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct on llama.cpp (commit 31288c9c6), RTX 5070 Ti (discrete). Every result is labelled transferable / discrete-only / prediction (D012).\n\n## What is here\n- `decisions/D001..D020` — chronological decisions with evidence (read D012-D020 first).\n- `LAB-FEASIBILITY.md`, `MANAGER-DESIGN.md`, `cc-inventory.csv` — Lab Manager findings and the CC inventory (observed vs inferred).\n- `bin/` — `run_op` (recorded commands), `lab` (image/job/attempt/cancel/reconcile/register/image-load/chaos), `perf_summary`, `index_evidence`, `cost_report`, `cuda_compile_check`.\n- `cc/` — Build CC (`build_engine`), `engine_handoff`, `routing_trace` (patch + replay), `memory_pareto`, `hybrid_expert` (Opus harness), `q8_reuse` (UNTESTED speed patch), `gpu_budget` (memory-restriction shim, may be incomplete), tests (`pytest` in each dir).\n- `evidence/*.jsonl` — raw per-agent streams (intent/started/outcome); `index/ops.jsonl` merged; `lab/jobs/*` job/attempt state + results; `experiments/` summaries; `claims/paper-claims.md` (15 source-supported claims, none tested yet).\nNot committed (reproducible/bulky): llama.cpp clone (`ref/`), image archives, nsys/ncu reports, base logits, traces (regenerate with the lab tests), Codex scratch trees. Models live in `~/models/campaign` (Granite pin 0da7a48b; GGUFs bf16/Q8_0/Q4_K_M/mixE4K/3K/2K).\n\n## Findings to trust (with caveats in the D-notes)\n1. Experts are 90.4% of weight bytes; mixed precision (experts Q4_K, rest Q8_0) halves Q4_K_M's quality loss at equal memory (D013).\n2. Static layer offload (`--n-cpu-moe`) cuts GPU MiB linearly but decode collapses (discrete-only, D014). Page-cache-as-expert-cache has a sharp cliff when RAM < working set (D015, contaminated by concurrent compiles).\n3. Granite routing skew is real vs a uniform control (D017), mild, weaker pooled across workloads.\n4. Hybrid hit/miss dispatch is bitwise-exact; the serial cost model holds (33 us/miss); perfect-overlap upper bound NOT supported (D019).\n5. Engine-native `--moe-cache-mib` (LRU, upload-on-miss) is slower than no cache until ~60% coverage (job-d50c052f94). The matched static-offload comparison in the same tool did not finish (D020) — rerun `lab/tests/static1.json`.\n6. Build CC: failures recorded (3 failed attempts), ccache makes patched rebuilds ~10-20 s; image identity bug found by independent observation (D016); real handoff `accepted` for the corrected record (experiments in `cc/engine_handoff/example-real5`).\n7. Lab core bugs found by testing recovery per phase (D006, D020); duplicate delivery, sandbox kill, retry-as-new-attempt, stale/conflicting result rejection all demonstrated (LAB-FEASIBILITY.md, MANAGER-DESIGN.md).\n\n## Unfinished (honest list)\nHard GPU-memory restriction shim (T-L) not compiled/tested by me; Strata concepts not yet applied end-to-end (only studied + CPU tests, and the single-layer harness); static hot-set expert placement (managed-memory idea, D018) not started; no end-to-end speed/memory result beats the baselines in a way I would call an engine win; q8_reuse patch not compiled; Opus/Codex